#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
TIS-6502: A TIS-100-inspired coding puzzle game using real MOS 6502 assembly.

Each node in a 2x2 grid is an independent 6502 CPU with 64KB of RAM and
memory-mapped blocking I/O ports to neighboring nodes and external streams:
  UP    = $E000
  RIGHT = $E001
  DOWN  = $E002
  LEFT  = $E003
  STAT  = $E004  (bit 0=UP ready, 1=RIGHT ready, 2=DOWN ready, 3=LEFT ready)

Programs are assembled at $0600 (or wherever .ORG says) and start at the
START label if defined, otherwise at the first instruction. BRK halts a node;
unused memory is $00 (BRK), so running off the end of a program halts too.

Solutions auto-save to ~/.tis6502/puzzleNN.asm (override with $TIS6502_HOME),
and best scores go to ~/.tis6502/scores.json.

Usage:
  tis6502                     # Launch interactive curses TUI
  tis6502 --test              # Run built-in assembler, CPU & puzzle tests
  tis6502 --list              # List all puzzles
  tis6502 --puzzle N --solve  # Run reference solution for puzzle N
"""

